Dear all,

I am just quickly giving some info on the project idea.

SymEngine <https://github.com/symengine/symengine> is a standalone fast C++ symbolic manipulation library, the idea is to wrap symengine into a R package to provide symbolic computation capacities within R. Also see the wiki page at https://github.com/rstats-gsoc/gsoc2017/wiki/Symbolic-Computation-in-R.

Isuru Fernando <isu...@gmail.com> is willing to mentor on symengine side, and is anyone interested to mentor on R side? Also for students who are interested, please learn about symengine from the wiki page <https://github.com/symengine/symengine/wiki>. The time left is not too much, if no appropriate student can be found, the project may be leaved to next year.

Best,

